Hiya Augustus! #game:mortemappear:0:0 #game:changeticksound:1:0
It's so nice to finally meet you! #game:mortemspritechange:1:0
...Though I guess Mote will be talking more to the player today. #game:mortemspritechange:0:0
I'm Mote! I'm one of the Mortems you'll be managing in this playtest! #game:mortemspritechange:0:0
Your job as the manager is to oversee the Mortems in your facility, and try to research them to their fullest.
You've got a few employees to start, and they'll be the ones you'll send out to perform the research. 
Let's take a look at what one might look like! #game:mortemspritechange:0:0
This is an employee tab. #game:backgroundappear:0:0 #game:shiftmote:0:0
Chipper fella, isn't he? #game:mortemspritechange:1:0
That top number is his BODY. It's how many hits he's taken, and how many more he can take. Pretty simple! #game:mortemspritechange:0:0
Below that is his MIND. It starts high, but various Mortems and effects can lower it.
If it gets too low, some seriously bad things can happen! #game:mortemspritechange:2:0
Next to that is their DISBELIEF. The better it is, the more it takes for an employee's MIND to decrease. #game:mortemspritechange:0:0
As we can see, Mark's DISBELIEF is... not great. #game:mortemspritechange:2:0
...Anyways! Last of all is their HEART! #game:mortemspritechange:0:0
HEART indicates how an employee feels towards Mortems as a whole.
Higher means they view them positively, and lower means they view us... pretty fairly, all things considered. #game:mortemspritechange:2:0
Most Mortems aren't nearly as nice as Mote...
You don't always want an employee to have a lot of HEART. Sometimes its better if an employee can distance themselves! #game:mortemspritechange:0:0
That's pretty much all there is to employees! #game:backgrounddisappear:0:0
During the day, you'll have the choice of where to send each employee. #game:unshiftmote:0:0
You can either assign them to a Mortem or send them to one of the training units.
When dealing with a Mortem, it'll be up to you to guide your employee through the process!
There are some Mortems where one wrong step can be disastrous, so your employees are putting their trust into you! #game:mortemspritechange:2:0
If you're worried about a certain employee, you can always choose to send them to training instead. #game:mortemspritechange:0:0
...That's everything Mote can think of! #game:mortemspritechange:1:0
Good luck Augustus! Mote believes in you!

-> END

